WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.501
-Welcome back, everybody.
Seth Meyers is joining us here.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:06.434
Congrats on the new book.

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:09.000
How is everything
on "Late Night"?

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.634
-It's great. As you know,

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:12.200
nothing like having
an audience back.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.734
It's so much fun.
-It's the greatest.

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:15.601
-It's the best.
-All that energy.

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:16.934
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:19.634
-But you're always --
I mean, when I first met you,

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:21.934
I know you did improv
in Amsterdam.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:24.167
-Yep.
-And you know a live crowd.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:26.767
You work off a live crowd,
but you became really good

00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:28.234
at delivering jokes
with no audience.

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:29.968
-It was fun.
I don't know if you felt this,

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:33.501
but when nothing gets a laugh,
they kind of all get a laugh?

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:34.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.467
It's impossible to bomb
when nothing's getting a laugh.

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:39.534
-Exactly right.
-They're all -- They're all --

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:42.334
-But no one can laugh, though.
Like, not even like Wally.

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:43.834
-Yeah.
-No camera operators.

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:45.901
-No, if someone --
If my wife accidentally laughed

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.267
in the background, I'd be like,
"Now you blew it."

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:48.501
-"Now you blew it."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:50.334
-"Now people know
these can be judged."

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:52.033
[ Laughter ]
-Exactly right, yeah.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.801
I saw one of
your day-drinking segments,

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:57.167
which are so funny -- Rihanna.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.868
And then you did one with Forte.
-Yeah.

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:01.234
-And I'm, like, "Oh, man."

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.133
-It was so --
I mean, you know Will.

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:04.501
You've worked with him as well.

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.400
It is so fun.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.801
I already knew he was fun to
drink with, so there was no --

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:12.033
There was no stress about
"How is this going to turn out?"

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.067
-Of course not. Yeah.

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.634
-It was crazy
that it counted as work.

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:16.767
-Well, he's one of the funniest
people on Earth.

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:19.767
And you did something where you
dared him to make you break,

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.234
to make you laugh.
-Yeah.

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:22.834
-And this happened.

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:24.234
And the Internet really --

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:25.367
This is bizarre.
He got right in your face.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.701
-Yeah, people pointed
something out.

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:30.801
-That is your nose.

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:33.234
Can we zoom in even --
Your nose is bent in half.

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:34.868
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:36.234
-Did you know your nose
could do that?

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:37.534
-I didn't know it could do that.

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:40.467
I think -- I saw that
and I think technically

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.834
I could fold it
into an origami swan.

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.868
[ Laughter ]
-Wow, that's a talent.

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:45.934
-That's a talent.

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:48.767
-Yeah, not many people
can do that. Wow.

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:50.968
And did he -- He broke you, huh?

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:52.033
-He broke me.
-Of course he did.

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:54.868
-I mean, he is --
The thing about Forte was

00:01:54.868 --> 00:02:00.400
never push him because his line
was farther than your line.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.300
-Always.
You do a bit on the show also --

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.000
off the show, but it's online,
called "Corrections."

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.901
-"Corrections," yeah.
-Which is very --

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:11.133
I think it's a brilliant idea.
Did it start from some fan?

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:14.434
-Yeah. So, you know, via Twitter
and via YouTube comments,

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:17.167
especially during the pandemic,
YouTube comments were, you know,

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:18.501
a hurtful and helpful way

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:20.434
of finding out
how the show was going.

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:21.567
-That's correct.

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:23.701
-And there was this thing
I did by accident.

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.400
I said "Legos."

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.767
And you're not supposed
to say Legos.

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:29.000
The plural of Lego is Lego.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.934
So you want to teach your kids
that so that that way,

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.167
when they say to other kids,
"Actually it's Lego,"

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:36.200
those kids will know
yours is an [bleep]

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:40.400
And that will just save time
for everybody.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.367
-That should be the next book.

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:43.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:47.033
-No, but it's Lego,
or you can say Lego bricks.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.234
-Ah. You can't say Legos.

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:51.501
-But it turns out there's a lot
of Lego fans out there

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:52.934
who were pretty upset about it.

00:02:52.934 --> 00:02:54.968
And so over the course of
three shows,

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:56.801
I kept trying to
correct the correction

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.000
and I kept getting it wrong.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.501
I said, "It's not --
You should say Lego.

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:01.834
It's Lego blocks."

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:03.734
And then they would say,
"Not Lego blocks, Lego bricks."

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:06.000
And I'm like, "It's Lego br--"
And then I realized,

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.067
oh, it's really fun --
the idea -- like, it sort of

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:11.334
takes the sting out of people
correcting you for tiny errors

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:13.033
if you address
every one of them.

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:16.567
So I do basically 15 minutes at
the end of each week on YouTube

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:18.334
where I just read through
YouTube comments.

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:20.133
And it's been actually
very informative.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.167
I'm learning a lot of things.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.267
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:23.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:26.868
-What's a favorite correction?
-So, for example, I heard

00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:29.634
Benjamin Franklin's wife's name
is Deborah,

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:31.767
and I said "That's really funny
to me 'cause that doesn't

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:33.767
sound like a Revolutionary War
name."

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:35.767
Like Deborah -- I would've
assumed the first Deborah

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:38.067
was born in like 1961. Anyway.

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:41.501
Then people said, "Actually no,
Deborah is a name in the Bible."

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:42.601
And I said, "That's shocking.

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:43.634
That would be like
if you heard, like,

00:03:43.634 --> 00:03:45.334
there was a Candace
in the Bible."

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:46.334
And then they were like,

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:47.601
"There's a Candace
in the Bible."

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:48.934
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:50.868
-Yeah. So when you do
corrections, you just realize

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.067
you're never going to get
everything right

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:53.501
and that gives you the freedom
to continue

00:03:53.501 --> 00:03:55.033
getting things wrong.
-Wow.

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:57.667
I wonder if people will find
something that you said tonight.

00:03:57.667 --> 00:04:00.634
-Oh, I'm sure they will. I
secretly buried seven mistakes.

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:02.834
[ Laughter ]
-That's why he's a genius.

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:04.367
Seth Meyers, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:06.901
Congrats on the baby,
and congrats on the new book.

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:09.067
Seth Meyers --
"I'm Not Scared, You're Scared"

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:11.300
is available now
wherever books are sold.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:14.467
And "Late Night" airs weeknights
on NBC right after us.

